Nix:

# Provides a patches to construct overlays for Go modules.
goModulesPatches = [
  # Map package import path to a set of patches.
  {
    path = "zombiezen.com/go/postgrestest";
    patches = [
      # ...
    ];
  }
  # ...
};

In Go, do `go list -m -json all` to list all packages. Needs `go mod download` to materialize the `Dir` field.

Better: In Go, run `go mod download` for the module path. Use Dir field.

Example:
{
  "Path": "zombiezen.com/go/postgrestest",
  "Version": "v1.0.1",
  "Time": "2021-01-26T02:23:43Z",
  "Indirect": true,
  "Dir": "/home/tie/go/pkg/mod/zombiezen.com/go/postgrestest@v1.0.1",
  "GoMod": "/home/tie/go/pkg/mod/cache/download/zombiezen.com/go/postgrestest/@v/v1.0.1.mod",
  "GoVersion": "1.14"
}

So match against Path and apply patches to Dir.

Note that overlays are limited in terms of files that can be modified.

See also https://github.com/felixge/go-patch-overlay/blob/main/main.go
